WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.530
At the science museum, children

2
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:04.570
under twelve pay half price.

3
00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.750
The ticket machine decides

4
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.250
your price in a blink.

5
00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:11.790
That decision is an if.

6
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.500
Today: decisions in Python.

7
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.620
A decision needs a question

8
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.420
with a yes or no answer.

9
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:22.860
Is age less than twelve?

10
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:26.570
Python can compare with less than, greater

11
00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:30.010
than, two equals signs for the same, and

12
00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:32.330
exclamation equals for not the same.

13
00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:35.090
The answer is True or False.

14
00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:38.690
An if line asks the question

15
00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:40.050
and ends with a colon.

16
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.940
The lines under it are pushed in

17
00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.760
by four spaces, and they run only

18
00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.320
if the answer is True.

19
00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:50.150
Under else go the lines for False.

20
00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.130
For more choices, add elif,

21
00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:55.650
short for else if.

22
00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:57.690
Under five, free.

23
00:00:58.340 --> 00:00:59.840
Under twelve, half price.

24
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.240
Everyone else, full price.

25
00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:05.330
Python checks from the top and

26
00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:06.930
stops at the first True.

27
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.360
You can join questions with and and or.

28
00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.530
With and, both must be True.

29
00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:16.890
With or, one is enough.

30
00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.400
A free ticket if you are under

31
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.120
five or over seventy.

32
00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:23.010
Quick check!

33
00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:26.130
With that program, a girl who is

34
00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.170
exactly twelve buys a ticket.

35
00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:29.730
What does it print?

36
00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:31.790
Full price.

37
00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:35.010
Twelve is not less than twelve.

38
00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:37.820
Mistakes like this hide at the

39
00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:40.280
edges, so always test the boundary:

40
00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:43.340
eleven, twelve and thirteen.

41
00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:47.160
The most common bug: one equals sign

42
00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.700
stores, two equals signs compare.

43
00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:54.330
If you write if age equals twelve with one

44
00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.110
sign, Python stops with a syntax error.

45
00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:01.180
Inside an if, you almost always need two.

46
00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.590
Decisions make programs smart.

47
00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:08.870
A quiz that says correct or try again.

48
00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:11.260
A game that ends when your

49
00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:12.700
lives reach zero.

50
00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:15.060
A phone that warns you when

51
00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:15.980
the battery is low.

52
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.540
In the app, open Logic gates.

53
00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:23.520
Try AND and OR with two switches,

54
00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.520
and watch when the lamp lights.

55
00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.730
Then solve the Door alarm: door or window

56
00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.890
open, and the alarm switched on.

57
00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:33.560
Your turn.

58
00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:35.170
Age is fifteen.

59
00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:39.680
What is age greater than twelve, and age

60
00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:42.360
less than eighteen: True or False?

61
00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:43.970
True.

62
00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.940
Remember: a comparison is True or False.

63
00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.880
if runs its indented lines only when True;

64
00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:55.720
else covers the rest; elif adds choices.

65
00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.400
Two equals signs compare.

66
00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:00.530
And test the boundaries.

67
00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.690
Try it yourself: write a

68
00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.150
quiz with one question.

69
00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:08.360
If the answer is right, print Well

70
00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:11.220
done; else, print the right answer.

71
00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:12.960
Test it with a right

72
00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.280
answer and a wrong one.
